      "MediaThumbURL" : null,
      "ShortDescriptionStr" : "The Wyoming Coop Unit is seeking an Associate Research Scientist to conduct research on ungulate migrations and support regional efforts to map and characterize migration patterns across Wyoming and the American West. The position will manage and analyze GPS collar data from multiple ungulate species and study areas, identify seasonal migration dates, delineate migration corridors, and develop spatial data products to support state and federal wildlife management and conservation efforts. The position will also manage and improve databases and analytical workflows supporting regional migration assessments, including ongoing efforts across the Greater Yellowstone Area. In addition to supporting established migration research and mapping initiatives, the Associate Research Scientist will contribute to and lead collaborative research projects that advance understanding of ungulate migration ecology and inform wildlife conservation and management across the West. ",
