      "MediaThumbURL" : null,
      "ShortDescriptionStr" : "The Alex French Lab in the School of Pharmacy at the University of Wyoming is seeking an enthusiastic, inquisitive postdoctoral research associate to join our team. The postdoctoral research associate will work on an exciting NIH-funded project exploring a novel signaling mechanism at GPCRs and its potential to transform drug discovery. The French Lab studies how GPCR signaling can be fine-tuned by agonists to maximize therapeutic effects while minimizing undesired effects. We are particularly interested in opioid and psychedelic signaling in the context of alcohol misuse. This postdoc will lead projects studying the mechanisms of beta-arrestin isoform bias at GPCRs and its consequences across the scales of biology. Our work integrates a wide range of techniques including protein engineering, high-throughput cell-based drug screening, cell and tissue microscopy, whole-cell patch-clamp electrophysiology, electrocorticography, and mouse behavioral assays.",
